From 9fee390a0085d11778e8bdf34945d2f6922c8112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:26:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): make status-bar controls hideable and default
 versions off [daveey]

User: "i dont need to see client and server versions"; follow-up:
"also, weve added a few other controls to the bar, they should be toggleable in the menu".

Why it happened: update awareness was coupled to permanent lockedVisible
version pills. The context menu consequently ignored hidden preferences and
disabled both version checkboxes. Why previous advice failed: synthetic
unlocked fixtures omitted production versionItem construction and concealed
the disabled controls. This is the recurrence of that failed hide instruction.

Remove version locks, retain Command Center as the locked recovery entry,
and migrate hidden preferences v2 -> v3 by adding just the two version IDs.
Retain v1 approval migration, unrelated choices, and subsequent explicit
opt-ins, including an empty hidden list. Register v3 as a shared preference.

Inventory all production controls: Command Center; connection/profile
switchers; backend health; sign-in; workspace; agents; cron; webhooks;
running/focused timers; context; cache; token throughput; plan usage;
system resources; approval mode; terminal; client/backend versions.
Connection/profile custom renders are now optional. Plan/resource toggles
stay discoverable while contextual rendering/polling gates remain intact.

Every contribution, including old render-only plugins, gets a checkbox via
explicit toggleLabel, text label/title, or a humanized stable ID. Preserve
existing declarative IDs/preferences, use registry IDs when missing, retain
render metadata and prevent plugins from locking themselves visible.
Discovered plugin controls: core-update, browser-focus, account-usage,
throughput, runners and CI, compute-rentals; bundled radio/hello-runtime.

Updater checks, progress, apply machinery, and Command Center's System
updateHermes action are untouched. Contextual availability remains distinct
from the user's persistent enabled preference. Reset hides versions again.

Proof on pool: baseline RED 9 failures / 33 passes; corrected production
contribution RED also fails with old panes source (locked data item cannot
hide). GREEN expanded desktop suite: 21 files, 128 tests. Renderer tsc passes
with shared vitest dependency resolved and bounded 3GiB heap. Targeted eslint
has no errors (one pre-existing projectTree dependency warning).
Full scripts/hermes-python scripts/check --base origin/main passed.
Production hook tests catch omitted menu metadata and any lock except
Command Center, actual version menu enables independent toggles, custom
render filtering occurs before mount, and preference migration/toggles
persist through module reload. No installed renderer verification claimed.

